{
 "encounter_id": "00659",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "UNKNOWN"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good morning, doctor. I've been keeping a note of this, so I can be precise. My heart pounds at night, and has done for about a month."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, that's really useful. Tell me what it feels like."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A thumping, in the chest and sometimes in my throat, quite fast. It wakes me up, usually between two and four."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long does an episode last?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Anywhere from a couple of minutes to, last Tuesday, I'd say twenty minutes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "[from the corridor] It was nearer half an hour, last Tuesday."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh, someone's talking out there. Ignore that. It lasted a good while, anyway."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll go by what you tell me. Does anything come with it, dizziness, sweating?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Dizzy spells, yes. Occasionally I feel light-headed when I stand up in the morning. I can't say when that began."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Roughly, before the thumping, or after?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I honestly don't know. I only noticed it recently."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fair enough. And do you sweat at night?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sometimes, after the thumping. My pyjamas get damp."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any chest pain with it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No pain, none whatsoever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you fainted, or come close to it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, never fainted."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What about caffeine and alcohol? Tell me what you have in a typical day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About four cups of strong tea, usually the last at around eight in the evening. And I drink wine at the weekend, a glass or two."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies to anything?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No allergies."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your numbers. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Please. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 74 and regular, blood pressure 124 over 78, temperature 36.6, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 14 a minute, and you weigh 66 kilos.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All normal? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All normal. Any cough or breathlessness at all?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, my breathing is fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any ankle swelling or tiredness, anything with the heart?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No swelling. Nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me listen. Breathe normally.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it a murmur? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your heart sounds are normal, no murmurs, and your pulse is regular."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's a relief. So what's causing the thumping? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Weighing it all up, the most likely cause is the caffeine, especially the tea late into the evening. I'd say caffeine-related palpitations."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I have been drinking more since I took on the extra project. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That would do it. Cut the tea down to two cups, none after noon, and see what happens over the next fortnight."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two cups. That will be a trial. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And alcohol late in the evening can trigger it too, so keep the wine to earlier in the day. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll bear it in mind. And if it doesn't stop? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep your diary going. If it gets worse, lasts more than half an hour, or you feel faint or get chest pain, come in straight away."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Understood. Thank you for being so reassuring. ~"
  }
 ],
